  <p>
    <em>Snake, 사랑방, Stand</em> explores the coexistence of unfamiliar
    narratives, domestic memory and symbolic forms through moving images. By
    bringing together elements that originate from different cultural and
    spatial contexts, the work questions how meaning shifts when familiar
    objects are displaced from their expected surroundings.
  </p>

  <p>
    Rather than presenting a linear story, the installation unfolds as a series
    of visual encounters in which memories, gestures and symbols repeatedly
    intersect. The viewer is invited to navigate these fragmented relationships
    and construct their own connections between image, language and space.
  </p>

